        <name>analog_offset</name>
        <qualifiedname>ndigo_configuration::analog_offset</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Configure DC offset values for ADC channels. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Sets the input DC offset-values to this value in Volts.</para>
<para>Default is 0.</para>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst:leading-asterisk
*          .. attention::
* 
*              After calling :func:`ndigo_init`, the ADC chip will heat up,
*              which will slightly shift its baseline.
* 
*              If you plan to measure very small pulses, wait for about
*              2 minutes after calling ``ndigo_init`` before you start
*              capturing data and set the values of ``analog_offset``
*              only after this startup period.
*          </verbatim> </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="ndigo_interface.h" line="257" column="12" bodyfile="ndigo_interface.h" bodystart="257" bodyend="-1"/>
