      <memberdef kind="variable" id="structndigo__configuration_1ab66c682cd186a6226dd8133b03ca55b8" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>int</type>
        <definition>int auto_trigger_period</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>auto_trigger_period</name>
        <qualifiedname>ndigo_configuration::auto_trigger_period</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Configure periodicity of the auto trigger. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Works in conjunction with <ref refid="structndigo__configuration_1ae7da8f7efc68e229b839523ec8310124" kindref="member">ndigo_configuration::auto_trigger_random_exponent</ref>.</para>
<para>The two parameters <formula id="0">$ M $</formula> = <ref refid="structndigo__configuration_1ab66c682cd186a6226dd8133b03ca55b8" kindref="member">auto_trigger_period</ref> and <formula id="1">$ N $</formula> = <ref refid="structndigo__configuration_1ae7da8f7efc68e229b839523ec8310124" kindref="member">auto_trigger_random_exponent</ref> result in a distance between triggers of</para>
<para><formula id="2">$ T = M + [1 \dots 2^N] - 1 $</formula></para>
<para>clock cycles.</para>
<para><formula id="3">$ 8 \leq M &lt; 2^{32} $</formula></para>
<para><formula id="4">$ 0 \leq N &lt; 32 $</formula></para>
<para>There is no enable or reset as the usage of this trigger can be configured in the channels.</para>
<para>To actually use this trigger, it has to be set as a trigger source in <ref refid="structndigo__configuration_1a69714f56a65985fa0ded10b4cee3dc47" kindref="member">trigger_block</ref>.</para>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst:leading-asterisk
*          See also :doc:`../functionality/auto_trigger`.
*          </verbatim> </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="ndigo_interface.h" line="336" column="9" bodyfile="ndigo_interface.h" bodystart="336" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
